1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,048
Welcome to the Pinewood Derby race manager.

2
00:00:03,048 --> 00:00:09,143
One laptop runs everything: it keeps the roster and results, talks to the track timer,

3
00:00:09,143 --> 00:00:11,695
and serves a web page for every job.

4
00:00:11,695 --> 00:00:15,310
The race coordinator runs the show from the laptop.

5
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:18,145
The projector shows the audience screen.

6
00:00:18,145 --> 00:00:21,406
The pit crew checks cars in from their phones.

7
00:00:21,406 --> 00:00:24,099
Judges pick design awards on a tablet.

8
00:00:24,099 --> 00:00:28,068
And a camera at the finish line records instant replays.

9
00:00:28,068 --> 00:00:32,817
All of it works over a local Wi-Fi network with no internet at all.

10
00:00:32,817 --> 00:00:37,070
This video walks through setup, race day, and every feature.

11
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:39,917
Race day starts with one double-click.

12
00:00:39,917 --> 00:00:45,835
Start Derby dot C M D installs what it needs the first time, starts the server,

13
00:00:45,835 --> 00:00:47,633
and opens the home page.

14
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:54,375
Allow Through Firewall dot C M D, run once as administrator, lets phones reach the laptop.

15
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:59,994
The first time you open the coordinator, it points you to the setup wizard.

16
00:00:59,994 --> 00:01:06,362
The wizard walks through nine steps and checks each one live: the event, the network,

17
00:01:06,362 --> 00:01:13,404
the projector, the phones, the replay camera, the timer, the roster, a dry run, and a summary.

18
00:01:13,404 --> 00:01:15,726
Green means verified right now.

19
00:01:15,726 --> 00:01:19,622
Amber means connected but something needs attention.

20
00:01:19,622 --> 00:01:21,420
Grey means not seen yet.

21
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:23,754
Everything needs one local network.

22
00:01:23,754 --> 00:01:26,155
A small router is the most reliable.

23
00:01:26,155 --> 00:01:29,623
The Windows mobile hotspot on the laptop also works,

24
00:01:29,623 --> 00:01:32,824
and the laptop then always has the same address.

25
00:01:32,824 --> 00:01:35,625
Phones scan a QR code to reach their page;

26
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:39,226
the codes are on the home page and on the coordinator.

27
00:01:39,226 --> 00:01:42,160
Phone cameras only work on a secure address,

28
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:47,229
so each phone does a one-time certificate install from the phone setup page.

29
00:01:47,229 --> 00:01:51,964
After that the pit crew and replay pages open the live camera directly.

30
00:01:51,964 --> 00:01:57,966
The wizard shows which phones are connected, whether they came in over the secure address,

31
00:01:57,966 --> 00:02:00,500
and whether their camera is available.

32
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:04,208
The roster tab holds the pack: dens, racers, cars.

33
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:10,586
Import a C S V from your pack spreadsheet, and the columns are detected automatically,

34
00:02:10,586 --> 00:02:11,847
or type names in.

35
00:02:11,847 --> 00:02:13,998
Each racer gets a car number.

36
00:02:13,998 --> 00:02:20,820
An open class for siblings and adults gets its own round and never races against the scouts.

37
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:23,713
On the setup tab, pick the race format.

38
00:02:23,713 --> 00:02:30,462
The default runs each den on its own, every car in every lane once, ranked by average time,

39
00:02:30,462 --> 00:02:34,540
then sends the top three from each den to a pack final.

40
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:39,806
Other presets race the whole pack together, by time or by place points.

41
00:02:39,806 --> 00:02:42,550
The format locks once heats have run.

42
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:45,952
On race morning the pit crew works from a phone.

43
00:02:45,952 --> 00:02:48,148
Find the car by number or name.

44
00:02:48,148 --> 00:02:50,133
One tap checks the scout in.

45
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:53,818
Type the weight; anything over the limit is flagged.

46
00:02:53,818 --> 00:02:59,770
Tap through the inspection checklist and mark the car passed, needs work, or failed.

47
00:02:59,770 --> 00:03:03,739
Take the car photo: the live camera shows a car outline,

48
00:03:03,739 --> 00:03:07,920
so every photo comes out the same shape for the big screen.

49
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,038
Record a few seconds of the scout saying hi;

50
00:03:11,038 --> 00:03:14,935
it plays in their spotlight and when they win an award.

51
00:03:14,935 --> 00:03:17,770
Walk-up racers can be added right there.

52
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:20,439
The race tab is the coordinator's home.

53
00:03:20,439 --> 00:03:21,192
At the top,

54
00:03:21,192 --> 00:03:27,968
the "on the projector" strip says what the audience is seeing and has one button for the next step.

55
00:03:27,968 --> 00:03:29,131
Click Start race,

56
00:03:29,131 --> 00:03:34,469
and the projector shows the round's title card with every car parading across.

57
00:03:34,469 --> 00:03:37,686
When the cars are on the pins, click Arm timer.

58
00:03:37,686 --> 00:03:41,724
The audience sees Next up, with one racer in the spotlight;

59
00:03:41,724 --> 00:03:45,899
the spotlight rotates so every scout gets one during the day.

60
00:03:45,899 --> 00:03:51,100
Click Start countdown: a drag race light tree runs, three ambers then green,

61
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:53,701
and the scout opens the gate on green.

62
00:03:53,701 --> 00:03:59,518
The timer reports the start, times pop in as cars cross, and the heat records itself.

63
00:03:59,518 --> 00:04:03,830
The result holds, then the instant replay plays in slow motion,

64
00:04:03,830 --> 00:04:09,031
then the next lineup appears with Now staging, telling the scouts who is up.

65
00:04:09,031 --> 00:04:10,263
Keep arming heats.

66
00:04:10,263 --> 00:04:15,670
When the round's last heat is done, the projector shows that round's standings,

67
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:17,860
and the button reads Next round.

68
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:22,312
Races have hiccups, and the coordinator has a button for each one.

69
00:04:22,312 --> 00:04:27,910
A car that does not finish: every lane still out shows a D N F button while racing,

70
00:04:27,910 --> 00:04:33,644
and after the heat timeout a prompt asks whether to record the D N F or keep waiting.

71
00:04:33,644 --> 00:04:39,175
A car jumped the track: Re-run this heat voids it and puts an identical heat next.

72
00:04:39,175 --> 00:04:41,940
A wrong time, or the wrong car on a lane:

73
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:47,336
Fix times lets you edit each lane's time and pick the car that was really there;

74
00:04:47,336 --> 00:04:53,002
the remaining heats re-plan themselves so every car still gets its full set of runs.

75
00:04:53,002 --> 00:04:57,994
A lane sensor dies: mark it out on the setup tab, and the schedule adapts.

76
00:04:57,994 --> 00:05:02,850
Every change is snapshotted, so an earlier state can always be restored.

77
00:05:02,850 --> 00:05:08,187
The replay camera can be a webcam on the race laptop, a laptop at the finish line,

78
00:05:08,187 --> 00:05:09,684
or a phone on a tripod.

79
00:05:09,684 --> 00:05:14,371
On the audience tab, tick "use this computer's webcam" and you are done.

80
00:05:14,371 --> 00:05:17,039
For a phone, scan the replay camera code.

81
00:05:17,039 --> 00:05:25,240
Recording starts just before the fastest car of the day could reach the line and stops right after the last car that finishes,

82
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,755
so a car that never finishes never drags the clip out.

83
00:05:28,755 --> 00:05:36,110
The clip is converted on the server and plays on the projector at half speed with the finishing order underneath.

84
00:05:36,110 --> 00:05:39,820
The coordinator can put any heat's replay back on screen.

85
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:44,620
Judges use their own page, usually on a tablet by the display table.

86
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:50,973
Add awards from the preset list, like Best in Show or Most Colorful, or type a custom one,

87
00:05:50,973 --> 00:05:52,597
optionally for one den.

88
00:05:52,597 --> 00:05:55,350
Select an award, tap the car that wins,

89
00:05:55,350 --> 00:06:01,421
and the card notes anything else that car has already won so awards get spread around.

90
00:06:01,421 --> 00:06:04,668
Speed awards fill themselves from the results.

91
00:06:04,668 --> 00:06:09,327
After the last round the coordinator clicks Start awards ceremony.

92
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:14,621
The projector shows the awards card, and each click reveals the next award:

93
00:06:14,621 --> 00:06:21,186
design awards first, then den champions, then third, second, and first place onto the podium,

94
00:06:21,186 --> 00:06:24,010
with the scout's video beside their car.

95
00:06:24,010 --> 00:06:26,368
Heat sheets, standings, the roster,

96
00:06:26,368 --> 00:06:31,287
and the awards list all print from plain pages linked on the coordinator.

97
00:06:31,287 --> 00:06:32,837
When rehearsal is over,

98
00:06:32,837 --> 00:06:38,228
Reset races on the setup tab clears every round and result but keeps the roster,

99
00:06:38,228 --> 00:06:41,799
so you can run the whole show again the next morning.

100
00:06:41,799 --> 00:06:45,573
Every screen you saw is a web page served by the laptop,

101
00:06:45,573 --> 00:06:49,144
so any device on the network with a browser can join.

102
00:06:49,144 --> 00:06:50,290
That is the tour.

103
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:51,570
Have a great derby.
